---
title: "Sale Lifecycle State Machine (Legion Protocol)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_created: Factory.create() + initialize()
    q_created --> q_prefund: FixedPrice: block.timestamp in [prefundStartTime, prefundEndTime)
    q_prefund --> q_alloc_period: FixedPrice: block.timestamp in [prefundEndTime, startTime)
    q_alloc_period --> q_active: FixedPrice: block.timestamp >= startTime
    q_created --> q_active: SealedBid/PreLiquid: immediately after init
    q_active --> q_ended: endTime reached OR end() called
    q_active --> q_canceled: cancel() by project
    q_ended --> q_refund_period: refund period active
    q_refund_period --> q_post_refund: refundEndTime reached
    q_post_refund --> q_results_published: publishSaleResults() / publishRaisedCapital()
    q_results_published --> q_tokens_supplied: supplyTokens() by project
    q_tokens_supplied --> q_claiming: investors claimTokenAllocation()
    q_claiming --> q_completed: all claims processed
    q_canceled --> q_withdrawing: investors withdrawInvestedCapitalIfCanceled()
    q_withdrawing --> [*]: all investors withdrawn
    q_completed --> [*]: sale complete

    note right of q_active
        INV-001: invest() only during active period
        INV-002: cancel only before tokens supplied
        INV-003: SealedBid has 2-step publish: initializePublishSaleResults() then publishSaleResults()
        INV-004: PreLiquid: project can withdraw capital before tokens supplied, must return on cancel
        INV-005: FixedPrice: prefund period -> allocation period -> sale period -> refund -> claim
    end note
